                <pb facs="0697" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.9312.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the American
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Instruct the American consul at Guaymas that he may, in so far as the local
                    authorities may permit him to do so and when such course appears to be
                    necessary, extend informal good offices in behalf of Chinese subjects.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
